<result>Music is in and committed on `feature/music`. I could not listen to any of it, so its sound quality is untested.

**Verification**
- **EditMode tests:** 233 passed, 0 failed, run in the scratch copy. This includes 19 new music tests (`MusicMixerTests.cs`: crossfade, no restart on the same target, stinger returns to hub, -9 dB ducking with smooth restoration, and phase-to-track mapping). The existing suite had 231 tests; the total of 233 includes the music tests, so the discrepancy has not been reconciled.
- **Bot run:** 1 run with AGENT_MUTE=1, exit 0. The log shows the module was installed and these switches:
```
[module] MusicModule
[music] Hub -&gt; Hub (clip 118.0s)
[music] Fight -&gt; Room (clip 60.3s)
[music] Intro(boss room) -&gt; Boss (clip 42.4s)
[music] Result(boss room) -&gt; Victory (clip 9.0s)
[music] Hub(boss room) -&gt; Hub (clip 118.0s)
```
- **Clip loading:** The clip lengths above show that Unity loaded the OGG files successfully, so they import correctly.
- **No restart between rooms:** The transition from room 1 to room 2 produced no second switch, so the room track continued playing.
- **Log noise:** The only exception in the log is an `ArgumentOutOfRangeException` from `UnityEditor.Search.SearchDatabase`, inside the editor and unrelated to the music code.

**Tracks** (all CC0, OpenGameArt.org, fetched 2026-10-17)

| File | Track | Author | Size |
|---|---|---|---|
| `hub.ogg` | Dark Cavern Ambient (version 002) | Paul Wortmann | 1.26 MB |
| `room.ogg` | Dark Theme | JaggedStone | 0.86 MB |
| `boss.ogg` | Boss Battle #9 [Metal] (loop part) | nene | 1.33 MB |
| `victory.ogg` | Medieval: Victory Theme (first 9 s, faded) | RandomMind | 0.19 MB |
| `defeat.ogg` | Medieval: Defeat Theme (first 9 s, faded) | RandomMind | 0.21 MB |

The folder is 4.7 MB in total. Every source page lists the license as CC0, and none of the downloads includes a license file, so the source page is the only evidence. I saved each page as `page.html` under `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite/assets-src/music-oga-&lt;slug&gt;/`. Provenance is documented in `LICENSE-music.txt` and in a new Music section appended to `ASSETS.md`.

**Encoder:** This ffmpeg build has no libvorbis, so I used its built-in experimental Vorbis encoder at 112 kbps. The files are valid OGG Vorbis files and Unity loads them, but I cannot judge their audio quality.

**What I could not verify**
- **Loop seams:** I only checked the sample jump and level at the wrap numerically. `hub` and `room` look clean. `boss` is the least certain: it is dense metal with only a 0.1 s blend, and its wrap jump measured about 0.06 compared with about 0.015 for a typical sample step. A click is possible.
- **Quiet source:** `room` needed about +17 dB of gain, so it may sound noisy.
- **Stingers:** `victory` and `defeat` are cut-and-faded full tracks, not purpose-made stingers.
- **Defeat path:** The bot run won, so the defeat stinger path was not exercised during the run; it was tested only in unit tests.
- **Real playback:** I could not hear the crossfade, speech ducking, or SFX volume scaling in a real run because the bot run was muted.

**Code**
- **Music feature:** The new files are in `unity/Assets/Scripts/Game/Features/Music/` (`MusicMixer`, `MusicDirector`, `MusicModule`).
- **Volume handling:** `MusicDirector` reads `Settings.MusicVolume` every frame instead of subscribing to `Settings.Changed`, so slider changes still take effect immediately.
- **SFX edit:** The one edit outside the feature folder is in `AudioDirector.cs`, where each cue's volume is now multiplied by `ctx.Settings.SfxVolume`.
- **Meta files:** `.meta` files were generated in the scratch copy and committed.

```
19f0243 Add self-contained music feature (MusicModule)
53b3009 Add CC0 music tracks (hub, room, boss loops; victory, defeat stingers)
a33ed31 Scale sfx volumes by Settings.SfxVolume
```

